<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Prince of Homburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1810">1810</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Prinz Friedrich von Homburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-prince">The Prince</a> of Homburg is a play by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-von-kleist">Heinrich von Kleist</a>, completed around 1810 and first performed in 1821. It is loosely based on Frederick II of Hesse-Homburg, who commanded the cavalry at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fehrbellin">Battle of Fehrbellin</a> in 1675. In the play the prince attacks against orders, wins the battle and is sentenced to death, and the drama explores the conflict between individual feeling and the law of the state.</p></div>
